WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.340 --> 00:00:08.400
This simple looking molecule holds the mystery of life!

00:00:09.020 --> 00:00:12.580
Right from modifying this white rice into a golden one

00:00:12.760 --> 00:00:14.740
to glowing these mice,

00:00:14.820 --> 00:00:17.920
this little molecule can make miracles happen!

00:00:18.480 --> 00:00:20.820
But how and why is this small wonder

00:00:20.820 --> 00:00:22.820
able to govern lives?

00:00:23.180 --> 00:00:23.720
Well,

00:00:23.720 --> 00:00:26.280
in order to unveil the hidden powers of this

00:00:26.280 --> 00:00:28.920
Deoxyribonucleic acid molecule,

00:00:29.500 --> 00:00:32.980
we need to first understand the molecule in and out.

00:00:33.480 --> 00:00:34.480
And for this,

00:00:34.540 --> 00:00:37.820
we need to dig through the history from the beginning!

00:00:38.260 --> 00:00:40.740
The molecule is best studied under the branch of

00:00:40.740 --> 00:00:41.960
GENETICS.

00:00:42.280 --> 00:00:43.780
So in the upcoming videos,

00:00:43.960 --> 00:00:47.240
we will be dealing with some basic topics in genetics.

00:00:47.860 --> 00:00:51.180
We will begin understanding the subject from its roots.

00:00:51.560 --> 00:00:52.900
So we will first learn

00:00:52.900 --> 00:00:55.560
how the foundations of Genetics were laid.

00:00:56.000 --> 00:00:58.540
Then we will get introduced to the remarkable laws

00:00:58.600 --> 00:01:00.440
put forth by Gregor Mendel,

00:01:00.460 --> 00:01:02.960
who is the Father of Genetics.

00:01:03.320 --> 00:01:06.800
These laws not only help us in understanding Genetics,

00:01:06.800 --> 00:01:10.440
but also have several real life applications!

00:01:10.720 --> 00:01:13.120
Later, we will get introduced to the concept of

00:01:13.160 --> 00:01:14.020
chromosomes,

00:01:14.020 --> 00:01:14.660
genes

00:01:14.660 --> 00:01:16.240
and the DNA molecule

00:01:16.240 --> 00:01:18.220
and what these are made up of!

00:01:18.600 --> 00:01:20.820
These structures in the living cell

00:01:20.820 --> 00:01:23.100
literally define the characteristics of

00:01:23.100 --> 00:01:25.780
all living organisms on earth!

00:01:26.360 --> 00:01:27.540
After this,

00:01:27.540 --> 00:01:30.320
we will talk about how the molecule replicates,

00:01:30.320 --> 00:01:33.920
and the theories put forth to explain that!

00:01:34.460 --> 00:01:35.240
Lastly,

00:01:35.240 --> 00:01:37.860
we will have a look at what happens if there are

00:01:37.860 --> 00:01:40.580
errors while replicating the DNA molecule

00:01:40.620 --> 00:01:43.380
or in the complete chromosome!

00:01:43.740 --> 00:01:44.560
That is,

00:01:44.780 --> 00:01:47.200
we will have a look at an interesting concept

00:01:47.200 --> 00:01:49.200
called “Mutations”.

00:01:49.720 --> 00:01:52.440
Let us understand the basics of “GENETICS”

00:01:52.440 --> 00:01:54.900
in our upcoming videos!

